---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Photo from '../../components/Photo.astro'
---

<BaseLayout title="A Welcome from our Lead Pastor | Pine Lake Covenant Church">
  <article class="page page--wide">
    <header class="page__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">A welcome</p>
      <h1>A Welcome from Austin Bailey</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="letter-layout">
      <div class="letter text-body-large">
        <p>
          When my wife Ashley and I moved our three kids—Ellie, Gwen, and Stephen—from Austin, Texas to Sammamish, we
          didn’t just move for a job. We moved because we felt called to be part of a community that was trying to live
          out something real.
        </p>

        <p>
          We’re what you might call “front yard people.” We love being outdoors, whether it’s family bike rides, rock
          climbing, or just hosting a bonfire with neighbors. For us, faith isn’t just something that happens inside a
          building; it’s about how we show up for each other in practical, creative ways.
        </p>

        <p>
          At Pine Lake, we don’t pretend to have all the answers. Life is complicated, and faith often feels more like a
          slow, steady journey than a destination. We’re simply a group of people trying to be a beacon of hope in a
          broken world — learning to be with Jesus, become like Jesus, and do what Jesus did.
        </p>

        <p>
          Whether you’ve been following Jesus for a lifetime or you’re not even sure you have a faith journey, you are
          welcome here. We care about being a place where family means more than just a demographic, and where community
          is more than just a social circle. It’s about belonging.
        </p>

        <p>
          You don’t have to have it all figured out to join us. Come however you’re comfortable — whether you’re all-in
          or still cautious — and you’ll find people glad to walk with you. We’re often gathered around coffee or food,
          and we’d love for you to join the conversation.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you’re looking for a place to explore faith at your own pace, we’d love to have you join us on a Sunday
          morning.
        </p>

        <footer class="letter__footer">
          <p>
            <strong>Austin Bailey</strong><br />
            Lead Pastor
          </p>
        </footer>
      </div>

      <aside class="letter-sidebar">
        <div class="letter-portrait">
          <Photo
            filename="Austin-2025-5-web.jpg"
            class="media__img"
            widths={[320, 640]}
            sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 320px"
          />
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .letter-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 320px;
    gap: var(--space-m);
    align-items: start;
    margin: var(--space-m) 0;
  }

  .letter {
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .letter p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .letter__footer {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .letter-sidebar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 2rem;
  }

  .letter-portrait {
    background: var(--color-white);
    padding: 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-soft);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-diffuse);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .letter-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-s);
    }

    .letter-sidebar {
      position: static;
      order: -1;
      max-width: 400px;
    }
  }
</style>
